2.9.26 - Data cleaning
Step 1 - Clean inflation dataset (load dataset, parse date column from daily to monthly, confirm CPI is on index level and not percent, sort and check for missing date values)
Step 2 - Clean daily coffee prices (load dataset, parse date column, drop duplicates, convert prices to numeric, make sure dates are in order, check for missing dates)
Step 3 - Clean daily oil prices (load dataset, parse date column, drop duplicates, convert prices to numeric, make sure dates are in order, check trading day gaps)
Step 4 - Align CPI to daily (each day ina  month gets the same CPI value, merge daily CPI to coffee and oil dates)
Step 5 - Deflate prices for coffee and oil (real price = nominal price x (CPI_base / CPI_t) -> CPI_base is the inflation rate in the first year in our timeframe, CPI_t is the inflation rate at the "current" timepoint
Step 6 - Clean climate data (load dataset, drop unused columns, parse datetime, convert variables to numeric, aggregate from hourly to daily to monthly, keep mean temperature and total precipitation)
Step 7 - Determine common date window (look at min/max dates for everything and determine final analysis wondow, drop all data we won't use)
Step 8 - Merge into master dataset (Merge daily coffee, then daily oil, then daily inflation, then monthly climate)
